{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310663,"nonce":"Xr5eYktx7IADgDm949WxUl4gx6I=","title":"OPEN, HIGH-SEVERITY, general (native Cranelift): a class field of type Null\u003cInt\u003e/Null\u003cFloat\u003e/Null\u003cBool\u003e immediately after a plain scalar ...","message":"**Repro:** `class Lin { var weight:Int; var bias:Null\u003cInt\u003e; function new(w,b){weight=w;bias=b;} }` then `new Lin(1,77)`. MIR shows `this.weight=weight` → `gep i32 $0,[1i32]` (elem_size defaults to 8, correct offset 8). `this.bias=bias` → `gep *u8 $0,[2i32]` — elem_size hits the `IrType::Ptr(inner) if inner==U8` branch → **offset 2*1=2** instead of 2*8=16 (object alloc is 24 bytes, 3 uniform 8-byte slots). The bogus offset-2 store lands inside the object's `__type_id` header. Result: `l.weight` prints `0` (should be 1), then **SIGSEGV (exit 139)** reading back through the corrupted pointer before the second trace even completes.\n\n**Root cause:** `compiler/src/codegen/cranelift_backend.rs:4067-4073`'s GEP `elem_size` heuristic infers \"byte-indexed raw pointer\" (elem_size=1) vs \"8-byte struct slot\" (elem_size=8) purely from whether the GEP's `IrType` is `Ptr(U8)`. But `Null\u003cInt\u003e/Null\u003cFloat\u003e/Null\u003cBool\u003e` boxing (hir_to_mir.rs:22624-22634) ALSO represents itself as `IrType::Ptr(Box::new(IrType::U8))` — indistinguishable from a genuine raw `*u8` field at this layer. So ANY class with a plain scalar field followed by a boxed-nullable-primitive field collides and gets the wrong stride.\n\n**Scope:** general — not specific to any one class shape. Checked nue's transformer/Linear classes for this exact adjacent-field pattern (scalar immediately followed by Null\u003cprimitive\u003e) — NONE found, so this is NOT the direct cause of [[bugs_nue_metaint_unbox_raw_enum_payload]]'s Bug #7 (the brk#0x1 trap after \"[gen] streaming...\"). Still worth fixing — any future/other class with this field order will hit silent corruption or SIGSEGV.\n\n**FIX DIRECTION (not yet implemented):** the GEP elem_size decision needs to distinguish \"boxed nullable primitive\" from \"genuine raw byte pointer\" — e.g. tag the IrType more specifically at construction (a distinct marker type for boxed-Optional vs raw Ptr(U8)), or thread the field's declared (pre-boxing) TAST type through to the GEP builder so elem_size is decided from the STRUCT SLOT layout, not the loaded value's post-boxing IR type.\n\nFound via a 2-agent cross-check (one hypothesized wrong-SymbolId field ordering, refuted; the other built the minimal repro and confirmed the elem_size root cause independently).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_null_primitive_field_gep_corruption` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}